# Line endings are normalised on the way in and checked out as LF everywhere.
# The repo is built on Linux, macOS, and Windows, and a file that arrives with
# CRLF shows up as a whole-file diff on the next platform that touches it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts are run by CI on Linux and macOS. A CRLF here makes the shebang
# line unparseable and the script fails with a message that names no cause.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the one exception. Windows hosts expect CRLF in these.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets. Marking them stops git from trying to diff or merge them, and
# keeps `git diff` readable when one changes.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.mp4 binary
*.ico binary

# SVG is XML and stays text, so a logo tweak is reviewable.
*.svg text eol=lf

# The two vendored forks are upstream's code, not ours. Excluding them from the
# language statistics keeps the repo's reported composition about vitrum.
vendor/** linguist-vendored
vendor-pty/** linguist-vendored
